1
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:10,920
-Built inside a glass house on a height in the forest near Lake Vänern beach.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,080
Could it be an example of the accommodation of the future?

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:19,800
At least it believes Anders Solvarm, whose natural villa has built the house.

4
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:22,400
Now we are in a wooden house, you might say.

5
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:26,280
We try to build with materials that store carbon dioxide.

6
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:31,080
Wood sucks the carbon dioxide in the air and then it is stored.

7
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:36,680
Actually, it is a regular residential building that we move in.

8
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:43,960
But when you go out into this space-

9
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:50,320
-Between outdoors and residential part, you end up in a garden.

10
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,040
Electricity and heat come from the sun during the summer.

11
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:56,480
In winter, batteries are recharged using biodiesel.

12
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,400
There is no connection to the mains.

13
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,320
-As they can tolerate a little frost.
There will be a little frost here in the winter.

14
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:04,040
It's just a single glass.
It rains, snows or never blows.

15
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,280
But it gets cool and cold in winter.

16
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:11,520
Not as cold as outside, but it can be minus degrees.

17
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,160
Almost SEK 8 million costs it for those who want to put the mittens on the house-

18
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,680
-As is currently out for sale.

19
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:22,600
The economy is that you do not receive any invoice.

20
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:27,640
So the house costs nothing, besides having to buy some firewood in winter-

21
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:31,160
-and some biodiesel to charge your batteries.

22
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:38,560
Extremely low operating costs.
In a longer perspective, it is often the large cost of the house.

23
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:43,280
Maintenance and operating costs are very small.

24
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:48,200
It is an expensive investment that pays off in the longer term.

25
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,560
When the really hot, hot summer days-

26
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:21,320
-We need to have shade.
Here we stand under a small shadow wall.

27
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:26,800
The best shade is obtained when the wine has grown up.

28
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:31,400
The wine is going up here.
In addition to the leaves giving shadow-

29
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:35,520
-So they transpire.
They are eating water vapor.

30
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:42,920
Then the temperature is lowered in the air.
Energy goes to evaporate.

31
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,040
Perspire.
It's kind of like when we sweat.

32
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:50,080
Then the temperature is lowered.

33
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:56,920
Shade, plants and ventilation, then it will be nice.
